@startuml

title Quality Attributes Affected by Deployment Decisions

!include ../../../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/structural/component-diagram-style.iuml

rectangle "Performance\n\nCo-location reduces latency\nDistribution prevents contention\nInstance sizing for throughput" as perf $fill_ok

rectangle "Availability\n\nRedundancy across failure domains\nNo single points of failure\nRapid detection and recovery" as avail $fill_primary

rectangle "Scalability\n\nStateless for horizontal scaling\nLoad balancing distribution\nElastic infrastructure capacity" as scale $fill_caution

rectangle "Security\n\nNetwork segmentation\nTrust boundary isolation\nEncryption across boundaries" as sec $fill_invalid

rectangle "Modifiability\n\nDecoupled deployment units\nStandardized patterns\nAutomated pipelines" as mod $fill_alt

rectangle "Cost\n\nRight-sized resources\nReserved vs on-demand\nOptimized data transfer" as cost $deep_caution

rectangle "Deployment\nDecisions" as deploy $fill_primary

deploy --> perf
deploy --> avail
deploy --> scale
deploy --> sec
deploy --> mod
deploy --> cost

note bottom of deploy
  Deployment architecture directly impacts
  system quality attributes through resource
  allocation and topology decisions
end note

@enduml
